---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import "../styles/projects.scss";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Vic Trodd ● Projects"
  description="View Vic Trodd's projects."
  page="/projects"
>
  <Fragment slot="highlight">
    <section class="highlight-container" id="projects-highlight">
      <div class="highlight">
        <div class="left-highlight text-highlight">
          <h1>Projects</h1>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="main">
    <section class="projects-content">
      <article>
        <h3>Aras PLM Data Cloner</h3>
        <p>
          A tool to export business data from Aras PLM to another Aras PLM
          instance, handling existing data and relationships between items. This
          tool was created to help supporters at CERN clone production data to a
          test environment.
        </p>
        <p>
          This tool sits on top of CERN's existing PLM UI and uses a custom
          built TypeScript API to communicate with the Aras PLM servers.
        </p>
        <p>
          Using this tool allows you to copy CAD files to the new instance,
          create new database items and new versions of existing items, and
          maintain the correct relationships in the structure.
        </p>
        <ul class="chip-list">
          <li class="chip">SQL</li>
          <li class="chip">C#</li>
          <li class="chip">React</li>
          <li class="chip">TypeScript</li>
          <li class="chip">SCSS</li>
          <li class="chip">Aras PLM</li>
          <li class="chip">XML</li>
          <li class="chip">REST API</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article>
        <h3>This Website</h3>
        <p>
          This was my first time using Astro, and it's definitely grown on me in
          that time. I wanted to create a website that was simple and easy to
          maintain whilst still handling complexity well, and Astro has been
          perfect for that.
        </p>
        <p>
          The site is still a work in progress, hence why none of these projects
          have any definition past some basic information. I will be adding more
          information in the future, but for now, I wanted to get the site up
          and running.
        </p>
        <p>
          10 out of 10. I would absolutely recommend Astro to anyone looking to
          create a static site.
        </p>
        <ul class="chip-list">
          <li class="chip">Astro</li>
          <li class="chip">SCSS</li>
        </ul>
      </article>
    </section>
  </Fragment>
</BaseLayout>
